{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalContentCasimir","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalContentCasimir","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.ContentCasimir","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QJucysMurphyEigen","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeWedderburnGeneral"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburn_contentCasimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburn_contentCasimir","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalContentCasimir.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**The content Casimir on the Wedderburn decomposition of `H_{n+1}(q)`.**  Under\n`heckeWedderburn : H_{n+1}(q) ≃ ∏_{λ ⊢ n+1} M_{d_λ}(K)`, `C_n` is the tuple of block scalars\n`Σ_{c ∈ λ} (q − q⁻¹)² [c][c+1]`.  Every block is covered, and no weight vector is assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.seminormalRep_contentCasimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.seminormalRep_contentCasimir","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalContentCasimir.lean#L66-L94","doc":"**Ram 4.1 applied to the content Casimir, on every seminormal block.**  `ρ_μ(C_n)` is the\nscalar `Σ_{c ∈ μ} (q − q⁻¹)² [c][c+1]` (cleared form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.cellCasimirVal_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.cellCasimirVal_eq","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalContentCasimir.lean#L55-L64","doc":"The same value written as a Laurent polynomial in the Murphy eigenvalue `q^{2c}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.cellCasimirVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.cellCasimirVal","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalContentCasimir.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The per-cell eigenvalue, denominators cleared: `(q^c − q^{−c})(q·q^c − q⁻¹·q^{−c})`, which is\n`(q − q⁻¹)² [c]_q [c+1]_q` with symmetric quantum integers. ","signatureChunk":0}]}